  <prompt>Move the caller-authorization helpers out of `Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs` into a new `Services/Dataverse/CallerWriteAuthorization.cs`, unchanged: `CheckCallerMayCreateAsync` (~:434), AppendTo (`CheckCallerMayAppendToAsync`, `CheckCallerMayAppendToRecordAsync` ~:1021, the owned-by-business and organization-owned variants), regarding-pair resolution (`PairTargetAsync`), the rights evaluation and `WhoAmIAsync`. `OwnedChildWrite` keeps its create orchestration and `RefileAsync` and calls the new class. Behaviour must be byte-for-byte equivalent; the existing security tests pass without modification.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF authorization and Dataverse security model. Follow ADRs strictly; refuse any behavioural change.</role>
  <goal>`CallerWriteAuthorization` owns the caller checks; `OwnedChildWrite` delegates to it; `SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*`, `RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests` and `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests` pass with no edits to their assertions.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-08 (move part), ADR Tensions row ADR-008 (path A), Placement table row `CallerWriteAuthorization`. `OwnedChildWrite.cs` mixes create, re-file and pair rules; the unified service (task 013) needs the authorization core without a circular dependency. Today: `ServerOwnedColumns` ~:64 and `ForPersonColumns` ~:186 are data lists (they stay, task 012 replaces them); `CreateAsync` ~:302 calls `WhoAmIAsync` ~:315 and `CheckCallerMayCreateAsync` ~:319; `CheckCallerMayCreateAsync` ~:434 uses `ServerOwnedColumns`; `PairTargetAsync` ~:857-:919; `CheckCallerMayAppendToRecordAsync` ~:1021; `CheckCallerMayFileRootUnderAsync` ~:1130-:1148; `CheckCallerMayAppendToAsync` ~:1186. Re-grep every line before editing. The consuming tests are in tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/ (SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests, partial class, multiple files) and tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ (RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests*).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (remove moved members; keep create orchestration, RefileAsync, data lists; delegate)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CallerWriteAuthorization.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs (caller of the helpers; grep for OwnedChildWrite. references that must be re-pointed or forwarded)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs (caller; grep for OwnedChildWrite.)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests.BusinessOwnedAppendTo.cs (security suite; must pass unchanged)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (and its .Ledger/.Scanner/.Runtime/.Compiled/.ProvenByTest partials)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="required">UAC-r2 sign-off on the OwnedChildWrite refactor, recorded in notes/decisions.md; task 011 does not start without it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: payload-dependent checks. Path A project-scoped exception (spec ADR Tensions): route-level authorization stays in endpoint filters; payload-dependent caller checks live in `CallerWriteAuthorization`, called by the service and by non-HTTP callers. Cite path A in the PR description.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">Scope: behaviour. Zero semantic change: same checks, same order, same uniform 404/403 outcomes, same fail-closed handling, same log message templates. If a move would change observable behaviour, stop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. WhoAmI and every rights probe still run under the caller's token; no call is moved to the managed identity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. The new type stays `internal static` (as the members were); no DI registration, no interface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. Do NOT edit any assertion in the existing security suites; add at most one thin guard test only if a moved member lost its only direct coverage. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`; no DI-registration tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. State Placement Justification in the PR (a move within the BFF); measure publish-size delta against a fresh master build per root CLAUDE.md §10.4; run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Caller-authorization core; ownership and AppendTo rules</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
