    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (security); confirm task 010's sign-off in notes/decisions.md; read spec FR-08 and the ADR-008 tension; run /conflict-check; re-grep every member named in the prompt and every external reference to `OwnedChildWrite.` (ChildRecordEndpoints, DataverseCreateRecordHandler, others).</step>
    <step order="1">Run the three existing security suites first and record the green baseline (counts) in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Create `CallerWriteAuthorization.cs` (`internal static`) and move, with documentation comments and log templates intact: the `Outcome` type if it is used only by the helpers (else leave and reference), `CheckCallerMayCreateAsync`, `CheckCallerMayAppendToAsync`, `CheckCallerMayAppendToRecordAsync`, the organization-owned and business-owned AppendTo variants, `PairTargetAsync` and its result type, the rights evaluation helpers, `CheckCallerMayFileRootUnderAsync`, and `WhoAmIAsync`. Leave `ServerOwnedColumns`, `ForPersonColumns`, `CreateAsync` orchestration and `RefileAsync` in `OwnedChildWrite` (task 012 and 013 replace the lists and the create half).</step>
    <step order="3">Re-point `OwnedChildWrite` and every external caller to the new class. Where an external caller used a moved member through `OwnedChildWrite.`, change the qualifier; do not leave a forwarding shim.</step>
    <step order="4">Build; run the three security suites plus RouteAuthorizationGuardTests; the assertions must pass with zero test edits. Diff the moved bodies against the originals (git diff --color-moved) and record that only namespace and qualifier lines changed.</step>
    <step order="5">Measure publish size against a fresh master build; run the CVE check.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any moved member cannot be moved without a behaviour change (shared private state, ordering between create and re-file, an `Outcome` type used by `RefileAsync`), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with options.</trigger>
    <trigger>If UAC-r2 has merged conflicting edits to OwnedChildWrite.cs since task 010, STOP, re-run /conflict-check and rebase before continuing; do not resolve semantic conflicts alone.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep for `CheckCallerMayCreateAsync`, `PairTargetAsync` and `WhoAmIAsync` shows they exist only inside Services/Dataverse/OwnedChildWrite.cs (a ~1.7k-line file mixing create, re-file and pair rules), called from ChildRecordEndpoints.cs and DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs through that class.</existing>
    <extension>This is the extension: the helpers are moved unchanged, not duplicated (spec §11 row `CallerWriteAuthorization`: Yes, moved unchanged). A new file is the only way to share them without a circular dependency between OwnedChildWrite and the unified service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The unified RecordCreationService (task 013) either references OwnedChildWrite (circular once the create half moves out) or copies the checks, producing two diverging authorization cores on the security boundary.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

